fter Amazon removal.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330790\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331523\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_urlbar_search.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_emptyInput.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_opensearchInstall.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_telemetry.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-switchTab/browser_closesUrlbarPopup.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_autocomplete_enter_race.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_restrict_keywords.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_restrict_keywords_autofill.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_restrict_keywords_autofill_locales.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_testUrlbarIcons.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_context_menu_item.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_topsites_sponsored.js"], "git_node": "cbd1f769b33dbdc78977c09e34334ecae6f8a159", "git_parents": ["c3bb37ca3f5ab3be3ac4e32d85125aad1d4eb6b1"], "node": "3a566be9b4c3a47ba1f330265fac6273a5dc9fa9", "parents": ["60fbbea381650078e11708080a4869c8377d52d6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791559983, "git_changesets": ["68e8e5e842d43711f3880432f81412401fb0bf09", "5661acd7c12feea6ea0941deb66fac3c3027f357", "4df1ceeb1bea637be12d0dcf36a5d2faa5e2b544", "c3bb37ca3f5ab3be3ac4e32d85125aad1d4eb6b1", "cbd1f769b33dbdc78977c09e34334ecae6f8a159"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "786": {"changesets": [{"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057143 - Avoid ProcessTypedArraysFixed re-entrancy by splitting Enqueue out of {Compress,Decompress}AndEnqueue and calling it afterwards.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nAlso fix up some spec references.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316356\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332445\n", "files": ["dom/compression/BaseAlgorithms.cpp", "dom/compression/BaseAlgorithms.h"], "git_node": "a1187ab5d1812d35e9fb576099b728b4825b4267", "git_parents": ["cbd1f769b33dbdc78977c09e34334ecae6f8a159"], "node": "58bcb19596d2f956b8c76c778005a72192792784", "parents": ["3a566be9b4c3a47ba1f330265fac6273a5dc9fa9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791567995, "git_changesets": ["a1187ab5d1812d35e9fb576099b728b4825b4267"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "787": {"changesets": [{"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065262 - Part 1: Stop the WebM init segment boundary running into a following init segment.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321725\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331616\n", "files": ["dom/media/webm/WebMBufferedParser.cpp", "dom/media/webm/WebMBufferedParser.h"], "git_node": "f053d6b2f94672649371c129c92e4ff280a09884", "git_parents": ["a1187ab5d1812d35e9fb576099b728b4825b4267"], "node": "d88c96a07ac2d4764d338211bb8224cee57e1376", "parents": ["58bcb19596d2f956b8c76c778005a72192792784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065262 - Part 2: Add tests for the WebM init segment boundary across back to back init segments.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321726\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331617\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestWebMBuffered.cpp", "dom/media/mediasource/test/bug2065262_init.webm", "dom/media/mediasource/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/mediasource/test/mochitest_compat.toml", "dom/media/mediasource/test/test_AppendMultipleInitTracksLast.html"], "git_node": "7c4afb7c4498bbf998c09ff2a8b825efbc516eb9", "git_parents": ["f053d6b2f94672649371c129c92e4ff280a09884"], "node": "78ad7b5290d3990967d713f091294f86baa91834", "parents": ["d88c96a07ac2d4764d338211bb8224cee57e1376"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568050, "git_changesets": ["f053d6b2f94672649371c129c92e4ff280a09884", "7c4afb7c4498bbf998c09ff2a8b825efbc516eb9"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "788": {"changesets": [{"author": "Josh Porter \u003cjoporter@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061552 - Add preference to hide the neterror illustrations.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe pref defaults to true. When it is false, net-error-card omits the\nillustration container, and the card shrinks to its widest text line,\nso the text stays visually centered instead of sitting left of center.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324950\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332066\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_feltprivacy_illustrations.js", "toolkit/content/net-error-card.mjs", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/aboutNetError.css"], "git_node": "883de3466ecf7f27084329e94812a6d1f60300f3", "git_parents": ["7c4afb7c4498bbf998c09ff2a8b825efbc516eb9"], "node": "531cdff6d865080a5428178d292e65bfada15df9", "parents": ["78ad7b5290d3990967d713f091294f86baa91834"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568089, "git_changesets": ["883de3466ecf7f27084329e94812a6d1f60300f3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "789": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lavindeep Dhillon \u003c62158930+lavindeep@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069768 - Declare subprocess fcntl as variadic and pass typed flags.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nfcntl takes two fixed arguments followed by variadic arguments. Declaring\nthe third argument as a fixed int passes it with the wrong calling\nconvention on Apple silicon, so the subprocess pipes end up with\nincorrect descriptor and file status flags.\n\nDeclare fcntl with \"...\" and pass ctypes.int values at the call sites.\nAdd an xpcshell test that checks the pipe flags on Unix.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323933\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332108\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_shared_unix.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_unix.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_unix.worker.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/test_subprocess_pipe_flags.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "95c55e51987372e5b4d1e106b2751d9174579f2c", "git_parents": ["883de3466ecf7f27084329e94812a6d1f60300f3"], "node": "300553b842917497b03cfe2c7a5845c51931c25f", "parents": ["531cdff6d865080a5428178d292e65bfada15df9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568142, "git_changesets": ["95c55e51987372e5b4d1e106b2751d9174579f2c"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "790": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069191 - Prevent socket thread priority events from blocking shutdown  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe shutdown could also have been prevented by a regular priority event, if it\ngets redispatched to the socket thread, or if it triggers the dispatch of other events\nto the socket thread.\n\nThe fix adds a pref to limit the shutdown event processing to 3 seconds.\nIf there are still events to be processed after 3 seconds, we go ahead and break from the loop.\nIt is possible this will cause shutdown leaks, but that's probably better than hanging forever.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327784\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331026\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsSocketTransportService2.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestSocketTransportService.cpp"], "git_node": "cec3097f53a2df67dc8f2b8dbfdd14368cdbb831", "git_parents": ["95c55e51987372e5b4d1e106b2751d9174579f2c"], "node": "b781a2231f8d82b89b6ccf282dfee9cc06053800", "parents": ["300553b842917497b03cfe2c7a5845c51931c25f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568221, "git_changesets": ["cec3097f53a2df67dc8f2b8dbfdd14368cdbb831"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "791": {"changesets": [{"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076648 - Clear previously-focused content after blurring due to caret move.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329959\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331215\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/focus/focus-navigation-starting-point-caret-browsing.html"], "git_node": "e46ef40bdabe255d020276a8baf656c5e7862f9b", "git_parents": ["cec3097f53a2df67dc8f2b8dbfdd14368cdbb831"], "node": "32acc5bf5bb22d5a945aed906a2bc037107e5069", "parents": ["b781a2231f8d82b89b6ccf282dfee9cc06053800"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568275, "git_changesets": ["e46ef40bdabe255d020276a8baf656c5e7862f9b"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "792": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070033 - Don't dispatch the message event when the worker global scope is null.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330138\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331519\n", "files": ["dom/workers/MessageEventRunnable.cpp"], "git_node": "e308698d20458105f641847cbada8dd13dadd94f", "git_parents": ["e46ef40bdabe255d020276a8baf656c5e7862f9b"], "node": "33b6ca37d8fa82ec83bb404ef68e635d1caa1fce", "parents": ["32acc5bf5bb22d5a945aed906a2bc037107e5069"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568314, "git_changesets": ["e308698d20458105f641847cbada8dd13dadd94f"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "793": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076235 - Only handle a pending seek in MediaFormatReader::UpdateReceivedNewData for the tracks being seeked.  a=RyanVM\n\nUpdateReceivedNewData skipped the audio track while a video-only seek was\npending, but not the video track while an audio-only seek was pending, such as\nwhen seamless looping rewinds the audio. If video received new data during\nthat seek while it had a decode request outstanding, it hit\nMOZ_ASSERT(!decoder.HasPromise()), and in release builds it would schedule a\nseek it was not part of.\n\nHandle audio-only seeks the same way as video-only seeks, matching what Seek()\nalready asserts for each kind of seek, so that a track that is not being\nseeked falls through to the normal waiting and internal seek handling.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329637\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331237\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp"], "git_node": "9ba362c3eed6c7bde5d82de04371d7ab58ade4e2", "git_parents": ["e308698d20458105f641847cbada8dd13dadd94f"], "node": "0dfe68b97e7372a18d4546d630a81f34f4e4a372", "parents": ["33b6ca37d8fa82ec83bb404ef68e635d1caa1fce"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791568345, "git_changesets": ["9ba362c3eed6c7bde5d82de04371d7ab58ade4e2"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "794": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053200 - Add SpecialPowers.prefEnv a=test-only\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314726\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/tests/Harness_sanity/test_SpecialPowersPushPrefEnv.html", "testing/specialpowers/content/SpecialPowersChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f6aa2159a3858647ca1a7f5ed97050fbf023f733", "git_parents": ["9ba362c3eed6c7bde5d82de04371d7ab58ade4e2"], "node": "02a2ed6bd937a42fbe7ec0d02c2e02639058e490", "parents": ["0dfe68b97e7372a18d4546d630a81f34f4e4a372"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065262 - Install the init segment files used by the WebMBuffered gtests. a=bustage\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "8704f66d2cab7b478d8867a2d76e395fd117db14", "git_parents": ["f6aa2159a3858647ca1a7f5ed97050fbf023f733"], "node": "fce03644eba06f81ff8ac45f107c296684e6b733", "parents": ["02a2ed6bd937a42fbe7ec0d02c2e02639058e490"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791573834, "git_changesets": ["f6aa2159a3858647ca1a7f5ed97050fbf023f733", "8704f66d2cab7b478d8867a2d76e395fd117db14"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "795": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019992 - un-reverse suffix-list diff.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nHG_SUFFIX_LOCAL is what's currently in the repo, PUBLIC_SUFFIX_LOCAL is\nthe new version we downloaded from publicsuffix.org.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323570\n\n(cherry picked from commit de3164f94d82811f263f7ab5362b5e27586384ff)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332562\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh"], "git_node": "937c71e1941dba48cfd7e474d4c6c84941dae434", "git_parents": ["8704f66d2cab7b478d8867a2d76e395fd117db14"], "node": "dda3f58279e76e92f9c484d9119d4030cdbad88c", "parents": ["fce03644eba06f81ff8ac45f107c296684e6b733"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1632517 - Validate every download in periodic_file_updates.sh before using it.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nThe compare_* functions are invoked as `if compare_foo`, and bash disables `set -e` for the entire body of\na function called in an `if` condition. A failed wget in those functions therefore never aborted the run:\n`wget -O` leaves a zero-byte file behind on an HTTP error, and the subsequent diff against the in-tree copy\nproduced a patch deleting the whole file. That is how D72155 came to remove effective_tld_names.dat, and\nthe suffix list and mobile experiments paths were still exposed to it. The remote settings path had a\nrelated hole, since `wget | jq \u003e file` without pipefail turns a failed fetch into an empty dump.\n\nRoute all downloads through a fetch_file helper that checks the wget exit status, rejects empty responses,\nand optionally requires a known marker to catch truncation. download_file wraps it and exits, so it works\nregardless of how the caller is invoked; download_json additionally validates the result as JSON. The ad\nhoc HSTS existence check is subsumed by the helper.\n\nRemote settings attachments are the one exception. A failed icon or bloomfilter download is not worth\nfailing the whole job over, since the task runs several times a week and will pick the file up next time.\nThose are downloaded to a temporary file first and only moved into place, together with their metadata,\nonce validated, so a failure leaves the in-tree copy untouched. The search-config-icons loop runs in a\npipeline subshell, so its exit status is now propagated explicitly.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324502\n\n(cherry picked from commit d5cc6447aea818ebfc6217ad2fb3e5dfebba99b2)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332563\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh"], "git_node": "115338cc032029126a7c5e2fcb8bda97c29be099", "git_parents": ["937c71e1941dba48cfd7e474d4c6c84941dae434"], "node": "c1d967ee74e2aa18d798163252e5b2d411f73d89", "parents": ["dda3f58279e76e92f9c484d9119d4030cdbad88c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1868149 - use moz-phab instead of arcanist in periodic-updates job.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283288\n\n(cherry picked from commit 6f7068b2be2f76eb99a652da957f31e3f024b744)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332564\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/setup.sh"], "git_node": "c2ffb056b835aa034cb139b5b75259db9babd1f6", "git_parents": ["115338cc032029126a7c5e2fcb8bda97c29be099"], "node": "190bae1ed2ffc5f07a877b699c1cc2a918131677", "parents": ["c1d967ee74e2aa18d798163252e5b2d411f73d89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071715 - pass --yes to moz-phab in periodic-updates job to avoid interactive prompt hang.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326107\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7cee42a08141cccfc7c52fa33c807cbc9646f2c6)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332565\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh"], "git_node": "f0b13e2e4d12a141e4b240fba150f39d8355f3a3", "git_parents": ["c2ffb056b835aa034cb139b5b75259db9babd1f6"], "node": "f4a2ab410de69f884f1b9b613cdc0747c49a4ba8", "parents": ["190bae1ed2ffc5f07a877b699c1cc2a918131677"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074975 - Record per-host HSTS probe results and failure streaks as a task artifact.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\ngetHSTSPreloadList.js now writes hsts-probe-results.json with the outcome, HTTP status, nsresult and latency\nof every probed host. The task gets an index route so each run can fetch the previous run's results and carry\nforward a per-host count of consecutive failed runs, from which the threshold for removing persistently\nunreachable hosts will be chosen. Only successfully completed tasks are indexed, so a failed or spot-killed\nrun never becomes the previous run. The count is recorded only; the generated list is unchanged. The promise\nchain in main() becomes sequential awaits, with the results written before keep-on-error rewrites the\nstatuses.\n\nA 2xx/3xx response without an adequate header does not extend the count, since the plan keeps removing those\nhosts immediately; a 4xx/5xx response without one (often a bot-blocking page) counts toward the threshold\ninstead.\n\nOnly hosts probed in a run appear in its artifact. A host that was not probed has left both Chromium's list\nand ours or become force-included, so its streak is dropped rather than carried forward.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328617\n\n(cherry picked from commit d9d6984e8fbe6f5163915b13cbbe7a14842fdabd)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332566\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh", "taskcluster/kinds/repo-update/kind.yml"], "git_node": "77ff1ecbae8cfffac6d8cd83141800ff8434ad04", "git_parents": ["f0b13e2e4d12a141e4b240fba150f39d8355f3a3"], "node": "17aa783f3109db4b94b5283f5ecad134a3f66afb", "parents": ["f4a2ab410de69f884f1b9b613cdc0747c49a4ba8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Probe HSTS hosts with a sliding-window pool and retry failures once.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\ngetHSTSPreloadList.js probed hosts in batches of 500 and waited for the slowest request of each batch, so most\nbatches took the full 30 second timeout. The bursts of 500 lookups also overwhelmed the container's DNS\nresolver and produced tens of thousands of false connection failures, which kept live Chromium-listed hosts\noff the list.\n\nA pool of 250 requests now starts the next one as soon as one completes. Every connection failure, TLS errors\nincluded, is then retried once in a second pass with the same concurrency and timeout. This replaces\nMAX_RETRIES, which at 1 never retried. Hosts reached on the retry are marked rescued in\nhsts-probe-results.json.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329494\n\n(cherry picked from commit 5807cfa561bec3d51ba6bf8df36ee112cbddfd70)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332567\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "59f9d572fea08aa4f8f48ecd3b994c7257c55429", "git_parents": ["77ff1ecbae8cfffac6d8cd83141800ff8434ad04"], "node": "d4cb347c34ba8f1a319b576acf50dcdca8e92931", "parents": ["17aa783f3109db4b94b5283f5ecad134a3f66afb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Keep HSTS preload entries whose host answers 4xx or 5xx without the header.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nA 403 or 429 bot-blocking page or a 5xx error page usually lacks the Strict-Transport-Security header that the\nsite otherwise sends, so whether a live site stayed on the preload list depended on the timing of the probe.\nSuch a response now keeps the entry like one that could not be reached, the same rule the failure streak in\nhsts-probe-results.json uses. A 2xx or 3xx response without the header still removes the entry, as does a\nheader whose max-age is below the minimum, whatever the status. The streak no longer counts the latter as a\nfailed run either.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329495\n\n(cherry picked from commit bf1c47e98ce0a2214a54018c065e34105199a6da)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332568\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "778031477d34a372669495c0f3f9830732d65747", "git_parents": ["59f9d572fea08aa4f8f48ecd3b994c7257c55429"], "node": "a1a2fa6d1aafcbd62469e3a532a1f0eb3dbd4663", "parents": ["d4cb347c34ba8f1a319b576acf50dcdca8e92931"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Probe HSTS preload hosts in random order and retry 429 responses.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nChromium's list holds thousands of domains of one hosting operator in a contiguous block, all served from two\naddresses. Probing in list order sent nearly every request in flight to those two addresses at once, and the\noperator answered with 429 for thousands of hosts that otherwise send a valid header, which kept them off the\npreload list. Shuffling the probe order spreads them over the whole run. The operator still limits the rate\nover the run as a whole, so this recovers only part of the entries it kept off the list. It also shortens the\nmain pass by about a third, mostly because that block answers slowly when probed all at once.\n\n429 responses without the header also join the connection failures in the retry pass, which runs after the\nmain pass and is spread out the same way. A second retry pass was considered and left out: it would cost about\nas long as the first, mostly in 30 second timeouts, while the first reaches under 1% of the hosts it retries.\n\nThis is an addition to the plan in bug 1891052, which did not cover rate limiting.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329496\n\n(cherry picked from commit 263339295e4694a4b9363552c6160184c69cca60)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332569\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "e8420cbaf593bbcb009d49e6b7c9961cb9a1d4ec", "git_parents": ["778031477d34a372669495c0f3f9830732d65747"], "node": "ff95dd4aa5b05624bb162ab5e3f71e850f86955b", "parents": ["a1a2fa6d1aafcbd62469e3a532a1f0eb3dbd4663"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078929 - Run the repo-update tasks on b-linux-medium workers with shorter max run times.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\npinning-update now finishes in under 30 minutes and periodic-file-update in under 6, and both took the same\ntime on b-linux-medium as on their current workers.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331399\n\n(cherry picked from commit fb57f2a08b3901528918878d0d262e7f51a8d199)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332570\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/repo-update/kind.yml"], "git_node": "168e82dc5a200cf5ecfbc302ed4f17f64af37799", "git_parents": ["e8420cbaf593bbcb009d49e6b7c9961cb9a1d4ec"], "node": "5ba21b92908f83c23d1a0ab98f7519db1d548e4c", "parents": ["ff95dd4aa5b05624bb162ab5e3f71e850f86955b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075888 - Make the repo-update tasks use git instead of hg.mozilla.org.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nThe repo-update checkout no longer forces an hg clone, so it clones from GitHub wherever the decision task\nprovides a git revision. Try pushes still get an hg checkout, so periodic_file_updates.sh picks git or hg from\nthe checkout itself instead of taking a --use-git option.\n\nThe in-tree files the tasks compare against (HSTS and HPKP lists, public suffix list, mobile experiments) are\nnow copied from the task's checkout instead of downloaded from hg.mozilla.org, and the unused hg repository\nmapping and clone code are removed, so -t is now required. Outside a dry run the script refuses a checkout\nwith uncommitted changes, because the update commit would include them.\n\nThe image now configures the ffxbld identity for both git and hg instead of the script passing it to hg\ncommit. Git refuses to commit without an identity, and moz-phab also needs one when it rewrites the commit to\nadd its trailer.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331279\n\n(cherry picked from commit 3d3cde2a8e0dd683015c284ec9bae29e67db2672)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332571\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/README.md", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/runme.sh", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/setup.sh"], "git_node": "788243c660ffd9433f43a0e9e42d8aab9cb69850", "git_parents": ["168e82dc5a200cf5ecfbc302ed4f17f64af37799"], "node": "6d252f8bd42317b5b819e5b516814e184f288444", "parents": ["5ba21b92908f83c23d1a0ab98f7519db1d548e4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075888 - Remove Thunderbird support and the archive.mozilla.org download path from the periodic update scripts.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nThunderbird does not run the repo-update tasks, so the product option goes too and the scripts use Firefox\ndirectly.\n\nThe --use-ftp-builds option is removed as well: no task passes it, and archive.mozilla.org has no\ntarget.tar.xz for it to download.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331280\n\n(cherry picked from commit 144feddfa83dcaf65e9917c2960370460f859295)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332572\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/README.md", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/runme.sh", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh", "taskcluster/kinds/repo-update/kind.yml"], "git_node": "b2832513b1c3491e45dfbcf84b3396f2396585f4", "git_parents": ["788243c660ffd9433f43a0e9e42d8aab9cb69850"], "node": "66a5ed1cb8fb14c3b304b07e29225fb170c8c892", "parents": ["6d252f8bd42317b5b819e5b516814e184f288444"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791576086, "git_changesets": ["937c71e1941dba48cfd7e474d4c6c84941dae434", "115338cc032029126a7c5e2fcb8bda97c29be099", "c2ffb056b835aa034cb139b5b75259db9babd1f6", "f0b13e2e4d12a141e4b240fba150f39d8355f3a3", "77ff1ecbae8cfffac6d8cd83141800ff8434ad04", "59f9d572fea08aa4f8f48ecd3b994c7257c55429", "778031477d34a372669495c0f3f9830732d65747", "e8420cbaf593bbcb009d49e6b7c9961cb9a1d4ec", "168e82dc5a200cf5ecfbc302ed4f17f64af37799", "788243c660ffd9433f43a0e9e42d8aab9cb69850", "b2832513b1c3491e45dfbcf84b3396f2396585f4"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "796": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Manuel Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066420 - Pass the untruncated update.status to pingStateAndStatusCodes() on the startup path.  a=RyanVM\n\n`#asyncInit()` split `update.status` and reassigned `status = statusParts[0]`\nimmediately after `readStatusFile()`, so the truncated state (ex. `\"failed\"`\ninstead of `\"failed: 7\"`) was what reached `pingStateAndStatusCodes()`. There the\nerror-code ping was gated on `parts.length \u003e 1`, which is never true for a status\nread off disk, so `AUSTLMY.pingStatusErrorCode()` was unreachable and\n`update.status_error_code_{complete,partial,unknown}_startup` only ever recorded\nthe three codes UpdateService.sys.mjs synthesizes itself (90, 91, 92).\n\nBug 1928229 introduced this by moving the split from after the ping call to the\ntop of `#asyncInit`. The staged path was unaffected because\n`#refreshUpdateStatus()` still pings before splitting.\n\nKeep the untruncated string as `fullStatus` and pass that at the ping call site.\nAll the `switch (status)` / `status ==` comparisons and `statusParts[1]` uses are\nunchanged.\n\nAlso key the error-code ping on `parts[0] == STATE_FAILED` rather than\n`parts.length \u003e 1`, so a failed status carrying no code records\nINVALID_UPDATER_STATUS_CODE instead of recording nothing. That matches what\n`#refreshUpdateStatus()` already does for `update.errorCode`, and it means a\nfuture re-truncation shows up in the data instead of silently emptying the probe.\n\nAdds `statusErrorCodeTelemetry.js`, which asserts the recorded samples for a\npartial and a complete patch, for a `failed` status with no code, and for a\nnon-failed status. Nothing in the tree asserted these probes before.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321460\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331019\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/sharedUpdateXML.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/statusErrorCodeTelemetry.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "7829953fdbfa9fc609a6e7273152ce4e2f22cc37", "git_parents": ["b2832513b1c3491e45dfbcf84b3396f2396585f4"], "node": "77fe6d9d7f95bda58463c6b51db506714e2cb586", "parents": ["66a5ed1cb8fb14c3b304b07e29225fb170c8c892"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791577569, "git_changesets": ["7829953fdbfa9fc609a6e7273152ce4e2f22cc37"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "797": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058860 - Defer removal of undeletable files during rollback.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThis patch improves non-staged updates rollback success rate by trying a\nrename-based strategy when deletion fails. On Windows a file can be locked\nagainst deletion while still being renamable, which is typically the case\nfor a binary that is currently mapped executable by a running program.\nPreviously the locked file was left with its new version contents, leaving\nthe installation in an inconsistent, partially updated state.\n\nThis strategy is already used by backup_discard, so we recycle it into a\nWindows-only remove_on_reboot() helper that moves an undeletable file into\nthe deletion directory and schedules it for removal on the next OS reboot,\nfreeing up the original path so the backup can be restored.\n\nAs a drive-by fix, we ensure that NS_tremove() failures end up with a\nwell-define updater status WRITE_ERROR_DELETE_FILE.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314881\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331156\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "5b1b723ceed168881a4c790798ccd3ffa34fd9f1", "git_parents": ["7829953fdbfa9fc609a6e7273152ce4e2f22cc37"], "node": "3784e2976ef9334823a0e6a5b0c8c8d428a112ee", "parents": ["77fe6d9d7f95bda58463c6b51db506714e2cb586"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058860 - Add updater rollback test for a file locked against deletion.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nAdds marRollbackFileLockedForDeletePartial[Zucchini]_win.js which reproduces\nthe condition addressed by the rollback fix on Windows: a new-version file\nthat is locked against deletion but can still be renamed, as happens with an\nin-use library or running executable.\n\nThe test injects the failure in TEST_UPDATER builds, making ensure_remove\npretend that removing the file named by MOZ_TEST_ENSURE_REMOVE_FAIL failed.\nThe hook sits in ensure_remove rather than in the rollback code so that the\nwhole rename_file fallback gets exercised.\n\nAlso adds checkToBeDeletedFileCount to the test harness. Since relocated files\nare named after a UUID, it returns them so that a test can check which file was\nrelocated, here by comparing contents with the new version of 0/0exe0.exe.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314882\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331157\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/xpcshellUtilsAUS.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marRollbackFileLockedForDeletePartialZucchini_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marRollbackFileLockedForDeletePartial_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "ca599112fe98d10279194b79e0773ee831547eaf", "git_parents": ["5b1b723ceed168881a4c790798ccd3ffa34fd9f1"], "node": "bf54b61afeb35116b87e72c7b97e7d09084a80e3", "parents": ["3784e2976ef9334823a0e6a5b0c8c8d428a112ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060275 - Factor out updater helpers in preparation for a new update phase.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nBoth AddFile::Execute and PatchFile::Prepare open-code the conversion of the\narchive item path to UTF-8 on Windows before handing it to the archive reader.\nMove that to extract_file and extract_file_to_stream, and let PatchFile write\nthe result of the patch to a destination that its caller selects through\nApplyPatchTo.\n\nThis is a pure refactoring, in preparation for a new phase that writes the new\ncontents of a file somewhere else than its final location.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317576\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331158\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "ce87d54fa0ab08e473bb32ecb736cdf3e0cc0f4d", "git_parents": ["ca599112fe98d10279194b79e0773ee831547eaf"], "node": "a78667a0b8d180cd14b494357b3c79b1839bd183", "parents": ["bf54b61afeb35116b87e72c7b97e7d09084a80e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060275 - Split the Execute phase of non-staged updates into Draft and Execute.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nNon-staged updates used to compute the new contents of a file and move it into\nplace in a single Execute step, so a failure partway through the action list\nleft part of the installation already replaced and recovery depended entirely\non restoring backups.\n\nAdd a Draft phase between Prepare and Execute. It writes the contents produced\nby every add and patch action to a .moz-draft file next to the destination,\nwithout replacing any installed file. Execute then only creates the backup and\nrenames the draft into place, so the installation is inconsistent only across a\nseries of renames rather than across decompression and patch application.\nStaged updates write into their own directory during Execute and have nothing\nto do during Draft.\n\nDrafts left behind by a crashed updater are removed before a new one is\nwritten if listed in the update manifest, and Finish discards any draft\nthat was never committed.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317577\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331159\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatedefines.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/docs/Implementation.md", "toolkit/mozapps/update/docs/Troubleshooting.md", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/complete_log_success_mac", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/complete_log_success_win", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_failure_mac", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_failure_win", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_success_mac", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_success_win", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "36b4869af2e9b8796411fd8d15e3da5f2209b09b", "git_parents": ["ce87d54fa0ab08e473bb32ecb736cdf3e0cc0f4d"], "node": "628f30bd1573ae13ecce218ab69c4f076a353251", "parents": ["a78667a0b8d180cd14b494357b3c79b1839bd183"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060275 - Test that the updater removes stale draft files.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nAdd marSuccessPartialStaleDraft.js, which seeds the installation directory with\n.moz-draft files as a crashed updater instance would have left them behind, and\nchecks that a successful update gets rid of them.\n\nAdd marSuccessPartialStaleDraftLockedForDelete{Add,Patch}_win.js, which make the\nremoval of the stale draft fail so that the updater has to move it out of the way\ninstead, once for each of the two callers of draft_discard. Both assert that the\nfile that ended up in the tobedeleted directory is the stale draft, by comparing\nits contents.\n\nAdd marStageSuccessPartialStaleDraft.js, which checks that a staged update never\ncopies a stale draft into the directory that replaces the installation. Staging\nlegitimately leaves the pre-staging installation directory alone, so the test\nremoves the seeded draft from it by hand before the checks that require that no\ntemporary file is left behind there.\n\nAlso make the check for temporary files that every updater binary test performs\nafter an update cover draft files, not just backup files.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317578\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331160\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/xpcshellUtilsAUS.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marStageSuccessPartialStaleDraft.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marSuccessPartialStaleDraft.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marSuccessPartialStaleDraftLockedForDeleteAdd_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marSuccessPartialStaleDraftLockedForDeletePatch_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_service.toml"], "git_node": "276e2ed02bd45bdf8f159687477b9391d26013a1", "git_parents": ["36b4869af2e9b8796411fd8d15e3da5f2209b09b"], "node": "1bce8a7acd26ed72e1d1cad0ab9ddb3fbe50dfbf", "parents": ["628f30bd1573ae13ecce218ab69c4f076a353251"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791577720, "git_changesets": ["5b1b723ceed168881a4c790798ccd3ffa34fd9f1", "ca599112fe98d10279194b79e0773ee831547eaf", "ce87d54fa0ab08e473bb32ecb736cdf3e0cc0f4d", "36b4869af2e9b8796411fd8d15e3da5f2209b09b", "276e2ed02bd45bdf8f159687477b9391d26013a1"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "798": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078358 - Ensure SharedSurface is valid before use.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe owning GL context of a SharedSurface is held in a WeakPtr, so it may\ngo away while the SharedSurface is still referenced. Make the IsValid()\ncheck detect this.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331421\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331886\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/SharedSurface.h", "gfx/gl/SharedSurfaceEGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp"], "git_node": "29e8403e3823cb17a0486040bb5cbadb35ffe172", "git_parents": ["276e2ed02bd45bdf8f159687477b9391d26013a1"], "node": "d0d714cb74134cd7f7b358c1da0bd1b07412b91a", "parents": ["1bce8a7acd26ed72e1d1cad0ab9ddb3fbe50dfbf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791577802, "git_changesets": ["29e8403e3823cb17a0486040bb5cbadb35ffe172"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "799": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078904.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331423\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331885\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/SourceSurfaceSkia.cpp"], "git_node": "6774a793749c3acb1443f3d780cc32aa65e69d97", "git_parents": ["29e8403e3823cb17a0486040bb5cbadb35ffe172"], "node": "3df92cbd2bbf2e8e312b55a1896fcab2c525d86d", "parents": ["d0d714cb74134cd7f7b358c1da0bd1b07412b91a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791577831, "git_changesets": ["6774a793749c3acb1443f3d780cc32aa65e69d97"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "800": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079065.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331497\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331888\n", "files": ["gfx/ipc/CanvasManagerChild.cpp"], "git_node": "c0b7d7f47acb8a62e0f9476815a2c32cfb087279", "git_parents": ["6774a793749c3acb1443f3d780cc32aa65e69d97"], "node": "