ft) We don't actually need this.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333398\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCEncodedFrameBase.cpp"], "git_node": "15927a2d6065e2326ed129337cf6a6a840a38fad", "git_parents": ["11ca93a86f32022ea85dc3723aab5b94f562f6ba"], "node": "42573bc5643899778d00ba8c7a2b057cb896fe12", "parents": ["8f5f8ef8465d783e2a718d3380c472cc57287c78"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791941028, "git_changesets": ["15927a2d6065e2326ed129337cf6a6a840a38fad"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "876": {"changesets": [{"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079171 - Update PlaybackEnded handling.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332012\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333290\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "084717e7db5c85bb25feaaf3f8794b4f0740c068", "git_parents": ["15927a2d6065e2326ed129337cf6a6a840a38fad"], "node": "3564ea786bb1b371b8da4e7a4b6aa6eb1f7b8524", "parents": ["42573bc5643899778d00ba8c7a2b057cb896fe12"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791941048, "git_changesets": ["084717e7db5c85bb25feaaf3f8794b4f0740c068"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "877": {"changesets": [{"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079156: Don't look up prototype for iterator helpers  a=RyanVM\n\nIterator helpers use a separate path in the spec that does not do a prototype lookup. This can be observable if %GeneratorFunction.prototype%.prototype is redefined as a getter.\n\nAsync iterator helpers are only stage 2. CreateAsyncIteratorFromClosure was removed from the spec due to lack of uses, which is why the comment points to an old revision.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331854\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333349\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/iterator/bug2079156-async.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/iterator/bug2079156.js", "js/src/vm/AsyncIteration.cpp", "js/src/vm/GeneratorObject.cpp"], "git_node": "4bbc9dff7c993697519f5940726dfa777dbc93a4", "git_parents": ["084717e7db5c85bb25feaaf3f8794b4f0740c068"], "node": "34048c08d340d1838b11d82588f273317bf2013c", "parents": ["3564ea786bb1b371b8da4e7a4b6aa6eb1f7b8524"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080210: Fix test for beta  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332486\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333350\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/iterator/bug2079156-async.js"], "git_node": "0c9d7885e31e6a34d4f83a5159c651fd444a5030", "git_parents": ["4bbc9dff7c993697519f5940726dfa777dbc93a4"], "node": "ade988a9bf294ad5994b1a584b4e2f26f5511727", "parents": ["34048c08d340d1838b11d82588f273317bf2013c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791941070, "git_changesets": ["4bbc9dff7c993697519f5940726dfa777dbc93a4", "0c9d7885e31e6a34d4f83a5159c651fd444a5030"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "878": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074097 - Prefetch AF_UNSPEC when Happy Eyeballs is disabled so the connection reuses it a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327845\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dns_prefetch_family.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "6a7ef9388cdb7b619963882f8b991d0288a7f0f3", "git_parents": ["0c9d7885e31e6a34d4f83a5159c651fd444a5030"], "node": "75515cac9f43787cb3d770f0f3638c2a801bbf96", "parents": ["ade988a9bf294ad5994b1a584b4e2f26f5511727"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946225, "git_changesets": ["6a7ef9388cdb7b619963882f8b991d0288a7f0f3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "879": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076410 - Read and close JSStreamConsumer streams on a dedicated task queue.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331070\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333133\n", "files": ["dom/fetch/FetchUtil.cpp"], "git_node": "4605b549281dc996a4816b0ab9a4ea9b2932a17a", "git_parents": ["6a7ef9388cdb7b619963882f8b991d0288a7f0f3"], "node": "ea3167a1065992bbc0257d5eafe5c11582122721", "parents": ["75515cac9f43787cb3d770f0f3638c2a801bbf96"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946788, "git_changesets": ["4605b549281dc996a4816b0ab9a4ea9b2932a17a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "880": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076271 - Make sure executor outlives stream parser.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nAlso stop the document load explicitly when canceling XHR.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331564\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333120\n", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestMainThread.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParser.cpp"], "git_node": "f6083f682ed5b7835d2c55513862db4636c12ba1", "git_parents": ["4605b549281dc996a4816b0ab9a4ea9b2932a17a"], "node": "98c4327d608a3f81d76095a239de56fcf5b0523d", "parents": ["ea3167a1065992bbc0257d5eafe5c11582122721"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946808, "git_changesets": ["f6083f682ed5b7835d2c55513862db4636c12ba1"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "881": {"changesets": [{"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079257 - Change txXPathNodeUtils::getPrefix.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332377\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333150\n", "files": ["dom/xslt/xpath/txMozillaXPathTreeWalker.cpp", "dom/xslt/xpath/txXPathTreeWalker.h", "dom/xslt/xslt/txInstructions.cpp"], "git_node": "231c2838a796004ba1f7e3cfc89c89493b636fe6", "git_parents": ["f6083f682ed5b7835d2c55513862db4636c12ba1"], "node": "b82bf2da1e60baefee2c6f2b9831af80f8476555", "parents": ["98c4327d608a3f81d76095a239de56fcf5b0523d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946828, "git_changesets": ["231c2838a796004ba1f7e3cfc89c89493b636fe6"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "882": {"changesets": [{"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061508: Remove this ancient stund compatibility mode.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332255\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333340\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/nicer.gyp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_build.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_build.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_client_ctx.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_client_ctx.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_codec.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_hint.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_msg.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_msg.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun_proc.cpp"], "git_node": "85f29b4c73216f229024f26d6c5068068eecddbd", "git_parents": ["231c2838a796004ba1f7e3cfc89c89493b636fe6"], "node": "24b83fa898ea1e59e1e4974aedc124ae33798ba0", "parents": ["b82bf2da1e60baefee2c6f2b9831af80f8476555"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946848, "git_changesets": ["85f29b4c73216f229024f26d6c5068068eecddbd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "883": {"changesets": [{"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073686 - Block scripts on ScrollbarActivity::BeginFade().  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330626\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333403\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollbarActivity.cpp"], "git_node": "dcedb47330e56148e78b4d919b15e749beffd9ee", "git_parents": ["85f29b4c73216f229024f26d6c5068068eecddbd"], "node": "23d077d4d9c469830ce3a0aa6a8c2bb94170c0b7", "parents": ["24b83fa898ea1e59e1e4974aedc124ae33798ba0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946868, "git_changesets": ["dcedb47330e56148e78b4d919b15e749beffd9ee"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "884": {"changesets": [{"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078727: Use release assert in RegExpStatics::executeLazy  a=RyanVM\n\nNormally, rerunning a regexp should get the same result. However, if there is a bug in the regexp engine that causes us to fail to match in a case where we should, *and* the choice to emit the buggy code depends on the frequency sampling that the regexp compiler does to its input, then discarding and recompiling can end up with a mismatch. We can nip it all in the bud by simply turning this assert into a release assert.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332218\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332786\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/RegExpStatics.cpp"], "git_node": "d0c6be2e625627eb52b5f72088dfbc1f97673c91", "git_parents": ["dcedb47330e56148e78b4d919b15e749beffd9ee"], "node": "59775bb604789a622b2b3398d1259e53e11bef15", "parents": ["23d077d4d9c469830ce3a0aa6a8c2bb94170c0b7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791946889, "git_changesets": ["d0c6be2e625627eb52b5f72088dfbc1f97673c91"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "885": {"changesets": [{"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080102  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332364\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333178\n", "files": ["image/AutoRestoreSVGState.h", "image/SVGDocumentWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "30e2fc5176befd2077949186d71b77d0b7b23b42", "git_parents": ["d0c6be2e625627eb52b5f72088dfbc1f97673c91"], "node": "12e879508c3f72d4993bbbed36b43d5a31afe3b0", "parents": ["59775bb604789a622b2b3398d1259e53e11bef15"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791949775, "git_changesets": ["30e2fc5176befd2077949186d71b77d0b7b23b42"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "886": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079676.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333187\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333447\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvasDisplayHelper.cpp", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvasDisplayHelper.h"], "git_node": "87f884d4968d0bcb5c428f5a0dbd952be67dd009", "git_parents": ["30e2fc5176befd2077949186d71b77d0b7b23b42"], "node": "a4af872c5dd8e63739084bf0af539d94bd302ea2", "parents": ["12e879508c3f72d4993bbbed36b43d5a31afe3b0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791949795, "git_changesets": ["87f884d4968d0bcb5c428f5a0dbd952be67dd009"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "887": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081467 - give the name \"unnamed log\" to CT logs without descriptions for now r=jschanck a=NPOTB DONTBUILD\n\nThis is a temporary fix that we should improve upon in the near future.\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getCTKnownLogs.py"], "git_node": "f7d4bb784b23b3a9802519bc2db0b2cb3c893891", "git_parents": ["87f884d4968d0bcb5c428f5a0dbd952be67dd009"], "node": "836282e000d3921df28f4631ce321721317eea67", "parents": ["a4af872c5dd8e63739084bf0af539d94bd302ea2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791980610, "git_changesets": ["f7d4bb784b23b3a9802519bc2db0b2cb3c893891"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "888": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054742 - Fix some incremental table layout issues during printing.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nContainer queries can cause some incremental changes which weren't\ncorrectly accounted for.\n\nRight now we don't allow fragmenting tables for multicol but maybe we\ncan after these changes.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312096\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333548\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableCellFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableFrame.h", "layout/tables/nsTableRowFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableRowGroupFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/table-container-query-crash-print.html"], "git_node": "73d48b80788926dae3592da4517499063fcb7d72", "git_parents": ["f7d4bb784b23b3a9802519bc2db0b2cb3c893891"], "node": "84d257b2ab660127ce5adef74940473372e86ba2", "parents": ["836282e000d3921df28f4631ce321721317eea67"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791980755, "git_changesets": ["73d48b80788926dae3592da4517499063fcb7d72"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "889": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055800 - Make nsTableCellMap::GetMapFor() better behaved.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312696\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333549\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsCellMap.cpp"], "git_node": "d6049cf18c5a878d96a1af48a2b64c9c7877f236", "git_parents": ["73d48b80788926dae3592da4517499063fcb7d72"], "node": "40f06dc8ffe1b036065715d0ba6cee3225a9b678", "parents": ["84d257b2ab660127ce5adef74940473372e86ba2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791980987, "git_changesets": ["d6049cf18c5a878d96a1af48a2b64c9c7877f236"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "890": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075432 - Ensure table continuations use consistent border-collapse model.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330808\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333194\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsCellMap.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-continuation-border-model-crash-print.html"], "git_node": "9d0ce9ab913f78cbeffe4eda4376ad7ca97df1a8", "git_parents": ["d6049cf18c5a878d96a1af48a2b64c9c7877f236"], "node": "3b3685b7b3afce47a48f6d59d61d272775102df0", "parents": ["40f06dc8ffe1b036065715d0ba6cee3225a9b678"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791981011, "git_changesets": ["9d0ce9ab913f78cbeffe4eda4376ad7ca97df1a8"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "891": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081570 - Disable HighPriorityRunnablesDoNotBlockShutdown on ESR153 triggering assertion  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333597\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/gtest/TestSocketTransportService.cpp"], "git_node": "24c226b66641bca1ef9d9fcfdf953b3c1181c6c4", "git_parents": ["9d0ce9ab913f78cbeffe4eda4376ad7ca97df1a8"], "node": "ba3b2160c0c1befb36be1556da69c38dba3c10ef", "parents": ["3b3685b7b3afce47a48f6d59d61d272775102df0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791981039, "git_changesets": ["24c226b66641bca1ef9d9fcfdf953b3c1181c6c4"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "892": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076332 - Only restore the backups that the current updater run created.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOn failure, every action restores the backup of its file whenever one exists,\nincluding the actions that never reached Execute. A backup left behind by an\nearlier updater run then puts back an old file next to newer ones. Each action\nnow only restores the backup it created. The backup that a precomplete remove\nshares with the add that follows it is restored by the remove, which rolls back\nlast.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329687\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333541\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialStaleBackup.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_service.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "240b96d5e48937665ea9291399fb05d930e75a7e", "git_parents": ["24c226b66641bca1ef9d9fcfdf953b3c1181c6c4"], "node": "8a885fb51916331cd37391071b915910501dc7a9", "parents": ["ba3b2160c0c1befb36be1556da69c38dba3c10ef"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791981236, "git_changesets": ["240b96d5e48937665ea9291399fb05d930e75a7e"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "893": {"changesets": [{"author": "eldjiikgull (EDS) \u003c333746118+eldjiikgull@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076744 - Check .onion names in their canonical form.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nStrip the trailing dots of the name and compare it without case before the\ncheck of network.dns.blockDotOnion.\n\ntest_dns_onion.js checks that each form of the name (lower and upper case,\nwith one or two trailing dots) is refused before any lookup when the pref is\non, and that the forms listed in network.dns.localDomains resolve to a\nloopback address when it is off.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329931\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333570\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/nsDNSService2.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dns_onion.js"], "git_node": "71f590985e4b072caf2bf687ccc12f0f8f9c8aff", "git_parents": ["240b96d5e48937665ea9291399fb05d930e75a7e"], "node": "783c92b47ecfca78e5dadd4071a6bc87eaf19132", "parents": ["8a885fb51916331cd37391071b915910501dc7a9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791981268, "git_changesets": ["71f590985e4b072caf2bf687ccc12f0f8f9c8aff"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "894": {"changesets": [{"author": "Simon Farre \u003csfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068362 - Eagerly compile event handlers only when IsSafeToRunScript for  a=RyanVM\n\nCurrently aDeferCompilation is only ever set for \u003cbody\u003e and \u003cframeset\u003e\nelements and the content attribute is one which is supposed to be\nforwarded to the window. nsXULElement also forwards to the window (so\nalso sets defer=false). This should only change behavior for those\nscenarios.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331252\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333603\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp"], "git_node": "74c43f3bee414f0c8b2174b4643dcc950f598255", "git_parents": ["71f590985e4b072caf2bf687ccc12f0f8f9c8aff"], "node": "4a3102544854a2537301c1145e6b0c2936fbf9f1", "parents": ["783c92b47ecfca78e5dadd4071a6bc87eaf19132"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791981446, "git_changesets": ["74c43f3bee414f0c8b2174b4643dcc950f598255"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "895": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081740 - Run repo-update-pinning-update on b-linux workers. r=releng-reviewers,jcristau a=NPOTB DONTBUILD\n\nb-linux-medium also schedules workers in northamerica-northeast1, where the task currently times out. b-linux\nonly uses us-central1 and us-west1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333631\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/repo-update/kind.yml"], "git_node": "2beab26a00b25ec5f689e9b96282a48732c4f499", "git_parents": ["74c43f3bee414f0c8b2174b4643dcc950f598255"], "node": "3eda69e446348720a051f8e05090958712c503d3", "parents": ["4a3102544854a2537301c1145e6b0c2936fbf9f1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983793, "git_changesets": ["2beab26a00b25ec5f689e9b96282a48732c4f499"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "896": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076332 - Remove the checkNoUpdateTelemetry call from marFailurePartialStaleBackup.js on ESR153. a=test-only\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialStaleBackup.js"], "git_node": "15643e9db8168b5e58d1b6bd68dbb3b91b926e69", "git_parents": ["2beab26a00b25ec5f689e9b96282a48732c4f499"], "node": "ac06c93db49283132812fc0337c7eae99eedbc87", "parents": ["3eda69e446348720a051f8e05090958712c503d3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791985131, "git_changesets": ["15643e9db8168b5e58d1b6bd68dbb3b91b926e69"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "897": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1781388 - Check every touch pointermove in test_getCoalescedEvents_touch.html and stop listening at pointerup. a=test-only\n\nOn Windows the injected touchmoves can reach content as a single touchmove, leaving only the first\npointermove's check, which was recorded by the popup's SimpleTest rather than the opener's. A compat mouse\nmove then dispatched a pointermove after pointerup, so the coalesced event checks ran after finish().\n\nThe test passes on Windows and Android, so both of its skips are removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333322\n", "files": ["dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/test_getCoalescedEvents_touch.html"], "git_node": "66789f50cb16dc644537b1bc9c65a4bd3cf75c7a", "git_parents": ["15643e9db8168b5e58d1b6bd68dbb3b91b926e69"], "node": "b071b4a18c703df9c18d9e2d8d36bc3a6246ac79", "parents": ["ac06c93db49283132812fc0337c7eae99eedbc87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1985017 - Run the checks of test_pointerrawupdate_event_count_touch.html at pointerup instead of waiting for a second pointerrawupdate. a=test-only DONTBUILD\n\nOn Windows the injected touchmoves can reach content as a single touchmove, so only one pointerrawupdate is\ndispatched and the pointerup handler waited forever for a second one. The coalesced pointermove is flushed\nbefore pointerup, so every event the test checks has been dispatched by then. The surplus-event messages no\nlonger increment the index a second time, which skipped every other event.\n\nThe test passes on Windows and Android, so both of its skips are removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333323\n", "files": ["dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/test_pointerrawupdate_event_count_touch.html"], "git_node": "407a21d5dc8b5b174e88cb1154cded0e12708014", "git_parents": ["66789f50cb16dc644537b1bc9c65a4bd3cf75c7a"], "node": "a5469b464dc5dcd53ea79bbf98f323ceb0eb2d29", "parents": ["b071b4a18c703df9c18d9e2d8d36bc3a6246ac79"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791986371, "git_changesets": ["66789f50cb16dc644537b1bc9c65a4bd3cf75c7a", "407a21d5dc8b5b174e88cb1154cded0e12708014"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "898": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081030 - Annotate fontface-descriptor-updates as passing everywhere. a=test-only DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-font-loading/fontface-descriptor-updates.html.ini"], "git_node": "098ce88c08ac16738581b028773b21cd135d30ee", "git_parents": ["407a21d5dc8b5b174e88cb1154cded0e12708014"], "node": "8257bbce5d3589f6876fe8998441f6708da5e1ac", "parents": ["a5469b464dc5dcd53ea79bbf98f323ceb0eb2d29"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791993328, "git_changesets": ["098ce88c08ac16738581b028773b21cd135d30ee"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "899": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080641 - More consistently deal with FontFaceSet promise resolution.  a=RyanVM\n\nDon't use the ready promise status as a proxy for \"do we need to\nschedule the resolve\".\n\nThis prevents .ready from resolving when other loads have started after\nthe fact already.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332819\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333531\n", "files": ["layout/style/FontFaceImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.h", "layout/style/FontFaceSetDocumentImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.h"], "git_node": "e2b47378c74673b033ba69dbb9f1f034f54d7c51", "git_parents": ["098ce88c08ac16738581b028773b21cd135d30ee"], "node": "67e111967fe4a927b98f8a43c7ac2083da902d4d", "parents": ["8257bbce5d3589f6876fe8998441f6708da5e1ac"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791993553, "git_changesets": ["e2b47378c74673b033ba69dbb9f1f034f54d7c51"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "900": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054363 - Mark the trackless-sender stays-muted subtest of RTCRtpTransceiver.https.html as intermittent on opt builds on ESR153. a=test-only DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpTransceiver.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "f943dac16672714cc95f9a45d0c6197e39a35641", "git_parents": ["e2b47378c74673b033ba69dbb9f1f034f54d7c51"], "node": "3ad5f1faa4db74a35100587b216c0b97da377dbc", "parents": ["67e111967fe4a927b98f8a43c7ac2083da902d4d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791995996, "git_changesets": ["f943dac16672714cc95f9a45d0c6197e39a35641"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "901": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dmitry Gozman \u003cdgozman@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076389 - Set the target of coalesced PointerEvents only after duplicating their private data.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nPointerEvent::GetCoalescedEvents() creates a DOM event that aliases an entry\nof the shared WidgetPointerEventHolder, assigns mTarget on it, and only then\ncalls DuplicatePrivateData(). The assignment therefore lands on the\nWidgetPointerEvent inside the holder, a plain ref-counted object shared by\nevery copy of the outer WidgetPointerEvent and never traversed by the cycle\ncollector. When a page keeps the pointermove event alive (hCaptcha samples\npointer events and calls getCoalescedEvents()), the target element and its\nwhole document are kept alive forever through that untraversed edge.\n\nSet mTarget after DuplicatePrivateData(), so the strong reference lives on the\ninternal copy that the cycle collector traverses. mWidget and mPresContext\nmust stay before it, since MouseEvent::DuplicatePrivateData() needs them to\ncache the event coordinates.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329732\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333815\n", "files": ["dom/events/PointerEvent.cpp", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/file_getCoalescedEvents_retained_event_leak.html", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/test_getCoalescedEvents_retained_event_leak.html"], "git_node": "585b7af18eb023c986df592b65d620afc0a112de", "git_parents": ["f943dac16672714cc95f9a45d0c6197e39a35641"], "node": "c3bc7ae6f11165b3cf5fea8de53056e1cef88ac9", "parents": ["3ad5f1faa4db74a35100587b216c0b97da377dbc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015119, "git_changesets": ["585b7af18eb023c986df592b65d620afc0a112de"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "902": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051358 - Fix mismatch between direct and indirect quad bounds.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe incorrect overlap was happening because with axis-aligned transforms we assume that non-antialiased quads exactly cover thir render task, meaning that the bounds of the indirect prim are the same as the bounds of the primitive that composites it. However the composite quad was more conservative (it was always rounded out to allow potential antialiasing pixels) so there was a mismatch whoch this patch addresses.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311284\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333578\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-fractional-overlap-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-fractional-overlap.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list"], "git_node": "6f5f7f44b784ebd7dc106a75bcb5fb0b380aa993", "git_parents": ["585b7af18eb023c986df592b65d620afc0a112de"], "node": "68238672fbd6d36c7306c706fc91e2eeefa75766", "parents": ["c3bc7ae6f11165b3cf5fea8de53056e1cef88ac9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051358 - Fix another seam in the quad code.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThis one was caused by add_pattern_prim doing an intersection between the rounded clip rect and the non-rounded local rect, which undid the rounding in some situations. The fix is to do the intersection earlier before rounding the clip rect.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311797\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333579\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "3bae15cbd6cdad8e366344e339dbc06f0b91e3bc", "git_parents": ["6f5f7f44b784ebd7dc106a75bcb5fb0b380aa993"], "node": "9cc5f6dd56b03dee25f034aecda93e0ba6702cd6", "parents": ["68238672fbd6d36c7306c706fc91e2eeefa75766"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015150, "git_changesets": ["6f5f7f44b784ebd7dc106a75bcb5fb0b380aa993", "3bae15cbd6cdad8e366344e339dbc06f0b91e3bc"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "903": {"changesets": [{"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051956. Treat a CRC error in a critical png chunk as a recoverable error so we keep the rows we already decoded.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nerror_callback keeps a list of libpng error messages we treat as recoverable. If\nwe hit one of those after a frame has been started, ReadPNGData terminates\nsuccessfully instead of failing, and we keep the rows we already decoded. Bug\n1873422 added that for invalid chunk types. CRC errors were not on the list, so\na wrong CRC threw the whole image away.\n\nlibpng hands us IDAT data as zlib produces it and only verifies the chunk CRC\nwhen it reaches the end of the chunk, which is what the spec recommends for\nstreaming decoders. So by the time the error arrives every row of a single IDAT\nchunk has already been written and we display the whole image. A CRC error\nbefore we have a frame, in IHDR or PLTE, still fails, because there is nothing\nto salvage.\n\nChrome and Safari both keep going here as well. Neither of them uses the data of\nthe chunk with the bad CRC, they stop at that chunk and paint the rows they\nalready had, and they don't fire an error event. Both of them reject a bad CRC\non IHDR or PLTE. A bad CRC on an ancillary chunk still discards just that chunk,\nwhich is what they do too.\n\nThe site in this bug uses a 1x1 transparent png with a wrong IDAT CRC as the src\nof every gallery image until it scrolls into view. The error event makes their\ncomponent replace the img with a fallback icon, and that img is the\nIntersectionObserver target, so the real image url never gets set and the slide\nstays blank.\n\nThe png spec allows either behaviour. It says that a CRC mismatch may be\nregarded as a fatal error, and that on a fatal condition a decoder should\noptionally continue displaying any image data already visible to the user.\n\nThe reftest and the wpt added here both load a png whose only defect is a bad\nIDAT CRC and whose rows all decode before that CRC is checked, so before this\nchange they fail and after it they render the same as the identical file with a\ncorrect CRC.\n\nTwo existing tests needed changes. createImageBitmap rejects with\nInvalidStateError when a decode failed, and images/undecodable.png only failed\nbecause its IDAT chunk has a bad CRC. The zlib stream in it is invalid as well,\nbut libpng treats that as a benign error, so with this change the file decodes\nto a blank image and createImageBitmap stops rejecting. Replace it with a file\nwhose only defect is a zero length IDAT, so the signature and IHDR are still\nvalid and the image still has an intrinsic size, but the zlib datastream its\nIDAT chunks form is empty and there is nothing to decode at all. Chrome rejects\nthe new file too. Safari decodes the old one and the new one, so it fails that\nsubtest either way.\n\ncss/css-flexbox/inline-flex-column-image-load.html came in from a WebKit export\nin bug 2033389 and was marked expected: FAIL when it was imported. The data url\nit loads is a mangled copy of a png that several other tests use, with a bad\nIDAT CRC, so we threw the image away and the inline-flex column had no intrinsic\nsize to size itself to. That was never a flexbox problem. It passes with this\nchange, so remove the expectation, and replace the data url with a correctly\nencoded 100x100 transparent png so the test no longer depends on how a decoder\nhandles a bad CRC.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318709\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333894\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsPNGDecoder.cpp", "image/test/reftest/png/green10-badidatcrc.png", "image/test/reftest/png/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/inline-flex-column-image-load.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/inline-flex-column-image-load.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/imagebitmap/createImageBitmap-invalid-args.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/images/undecodable.png", "testing/web-platform/tests/png/errors/idat-crc-error-recovery.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/png/errors/support/bad-idat-crc.png"], "git_node": "01af27fb059c76dc55c890390fda4c8841786d5d", "git_parents": ["3bae15cbd6cdad8e366344e339dbc06f0b91e3bc"], "node": "fd1401f9310efcf373ca992a50b861026040bf09", "parents": ["9cc5f6dd56b03dee25f034aecda93e0ba6702cd6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015180, "git_changesets": ["01af27fb059c76dc55c890390fda4c8841786d5d"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "904": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1661556 - Iterate the action list in reverse order on rollback.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe updater's rollback code currently implicitly assumes that no two actions\never touch the same path. Non-staged complete updates break this assumption by\nmaking us perform a REMOVE (from the precomplete actions) followed by an ADD,\nincluding on firefox.exe. The consequence is that an update failure results in\nfile loss for the affected paths, so an install directory ends up without\nfirefox.exe in particular.\n\nIterating in reverse order during rollback fixes this. AddFile::Finish now runs\nfirst: it removes the file it added, then finds the shared backup slot still\npopulated and restores the original. RemoveFile::Finish then finds the slot\nalready consumed and does nothing, leaving the restored original in place. This\nimplements the common sense idea that we want to first undo what we did last.\n\nThe success path keeps the forward order, because there RemoveDir::Finish is\nwhat actually removes the directories and it must visit children before their\nparents.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318734\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333689\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_failure_mac", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/partial_log_failure_win", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "c4d8da3fa17e1c94af9883c258c2432c59786e66", "git_parents": ["01af27fb059c76dc55c890390fda4c8841786d5d"], "node": "c642ee7c5be830fea37887d6af8dd603fd78a118", "parents": ["fd1401f9310efcf373ca992a50b861026040bf09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1661556 - Test rollback of a failed non-staged complete update.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe new test exercises the path that the previous patch fixes: a non-staged\ncomplete update where the installed precomplete manifest removes files that the\nMAR manifest then adds back.\n\ncheckFilesAfterUpdateFailure verifies that the whole installation is back to\nits original contents. Without the previous patch, the removed-then-added files\nare missing instead of restored and the test fails. The failure is injected\nafter those re-adds have run, by locking 1/10/10text0.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318735\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333690\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marRemoveAddRollbackFailureComplete_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml"], "git_node": "71d6611c86d3e0a1155f730cdf239f768fbcc85a", "git_parents": ["c4d8da3fa17e1c94af9883c258c2432c59786e66"], "node": "17d90c064d45947e6946c805a36e6c31802edbc8", "parents": ["c642ee7c5be830fea37887d6af8dd603fd78a118"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015208, "git_changesets": ["c4d8da3fa17e1c94af9883c258c2432c59786e66", "71d6611c86d3e0a1155f730cdf239f768fbcc85a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "905": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069536: Allow Firefox to start if the profile data directories are inaccessible.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326501\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333624\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/profile/nsToolkitProfileService.cpp", "toolkit/profile/nsToolkitProfileService.h", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_unreadable_ini.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_unreadable_ini_createprofile.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_unreadable_ini_no_profile.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_unreadable_ini_p.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_unreadable_ini_profilemanager.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "c7e2826d7cf5e43f2c67ee6a3b77df603515b432", "git_parents": ["71d6611c86d3e0a1155f730cdf239f768fbcc85a"], "node": "b07ca0ae0ac7933da22179fb76ab29d90cc66392", "parents": ["17d90c064d45947e6946c805a36e6c31802edbc8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015236, "git_changesets": ["c7e2826d7cf5e43f2c67ee6a3b77df603515b432"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "906": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076267 - Ensure proper node iteration.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330606\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333872\n", "files": ["dom/base/NodeIterator.cpp", "dom/base/NodeIterator.h"], "git_node": "8767e8aff61ef49b6facbfa0ee53d431a08946ec", "git_parents": ["c7e2826d7cf5e43f2c67ee6a3b77df603515b432"], "node": "011934f8f8cab01685d0cfbd4847c10cc544d7e2", "parents": ["b07ca0ae0ac7933da22179fb76ab29d90cc66392"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015291, "git_changesets": ["8767e8aff61ef49b6facbfa0ee53d431a08946ec"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "907": {"changesets": [{"author": "hsingh-moz \u003c105445818+hsingh-moz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072411 - Guard DecryptingInputStream state with a mutex.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328575\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331656\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream.cpp", "dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream.h", "dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream_impl.h"], "git_node": "ead64c9fb3e24721cf64d93c48ca1e484f57d3d8", "git_parents": ["8767e8aff61ef49b6facbfa0ee53d431a08946ec"], "node": "4d017b53ba8106f0d48c4c4e1645647123d1b4d5", "parents": ["011934f8f8cab01685d0cfbd4847c10cc544d7e2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015315, "git_changesets": ["ead64c9fb3e24721cf64d93c48ca1e484f57d3d8"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "908": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076705, ensure the right node document,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330760\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333874\n", "files": ["dom/xml/nsXMLContentSink.cpp"], "git_node": "f974d7e5f33ed99afb3d8f65ec23115370246b91", "git_parents": ["ead64c9fb3e24721cf64d93c48ca1e484f57d3d8"], "node": "d2de901ef5f5ef7330bfef06a613d7d9b2a6e30e", "parents": ["4d017b53ba8106f0d48c4c4e1645647123d1b4d5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792015338, "git_changesets": ["f974d7e5f33ed99afb3d8f65ec23115370246b91"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "909": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077385, ensure right cell index is returned,  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330564\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333882\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLTableCellElement.cpp"], "git_node": "503b35a8ecaccf7dfcfe1c3ccd19edb7fcaa7160", "git_parents": ["f974d7e5f33ed99afb3d8f65ec23115370246b91"], "node": "76dc7db87e4b4901b2b4c3065cbdc64f243e6121", "parents": ["d2de901ef5f5ef7330bfef06a613d7d9b2a6e30e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792016106, "git_changesets": ["503b35a8ecaccf7dfcfe1c3ccd19edb7fcaa7160"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "910": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061857 - Part 1: Add customization options to SyncedContext,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThis is a new declarative way to describe when fields are allowed to be\nset, which should simplify future changes to CanSet and encourage people\nto specify restrictions on newly added synced fields.\n\nThis is just an initial set of customization fields, which can be\nexpanded upon in the future.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317549\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333555\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/SyncedContext.h", "docshell/base/SyncedContextInlines.h", "docshell/base/WindowContext.h"], "git_node": "210f7cbf321512d55fc6d04dcbf95f0b8774fd6b", "git_parents": ["503b35a8ecaccf7dfcfe1c3ccd19edb7fcaa7160"], "node": "a7d5d548d271a6440471d632d421c8572abee303", "parents": ["76dc7db87e4b4901b2b4c3065cbdc64f243e6121"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061857 - Part 2: Migrate existing synced fields to use customization options,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317550\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333556\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp", "docshell/base/WindowContext.h"], "git_node": "62c3cc4da97ffb7f227fb9b6b55da3d204564fd6", "git_parents": ["210f7cbf321512d55fc6d04dcbf95f0b8774fd6b"], "node": "4850fe29ec7d6fdb597206ab668baaecb45e2bca", "parents": ["a7d5d548d271a6440471d632d421c8572abee303"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061857 - Part 3: Allow configuring synced field defaults,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https